  "question": {
    "text": "Sometimes it is convenient to construct a system of units so that all quantities can be expressed in terms of only one physical quantity. In one such system, dimensions of different quantities are given in terms of a quantity&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math> as follows: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>position</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></msup></mfenced><mo>;</mo></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>speed</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>&#946;</mi></msup></mfenced></math>;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>acceleration</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mfenced></math>;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>linear</mi><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi>momentum</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>q</mi></msup></mfenced></math>;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>force</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mfenced></math>.&nbsp;Then",
